 [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduced independently on 2026-11-04 while verifying upset-prissy-olm. make verify's integration tier crashed xdist worker gw2 on test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass. Run alone: 307.5 s wall (user 15.8 s, sys 28.3 s) on the branch, and 306.9 s (user 13.3 s, sys 23.5 s) on its parent e0ab18822c6 (origin/main), both rc=1 at the 300 s timeout, load average 30-36. The test times out with or without the opcert change, and wall time far exceeds CPU time, which is consistent with waiting on child processes.","timestamp":1793792495268776001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause, measured 2026-11-04 on origin/main 30f06afc412 (macOS host, load average 28-36).\n\nBaseline: the benchmark test run alone took 310.0 s wall (user 17.8 s, sys 31.0 s), rc=1 at the 300 s timeout. The timeout stack was in the per-comment cross-session read (`emit_cross_session_warning` -> `show_ticket` -> reduce).\n\nGit child processes by caller, `rebar.import_tickets` with n=50 tickets, 1 comment each:\n- Acting session id set (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, as in any agent shell): 120 git processes, 15.8 s wall. 100 of them are 2 per comment, both in `ensure_fresh` under the warning's `show_ticket`: `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (repo_root_or_none) and `git rev-parse --verify <branch>`.\n- No session id (all 4 session vars unset, as in CI): 19 git processes, 3.2 s wall. `cross_session_warning_for` returns before the read when no session id is set.\n\nThat is why CI passes in about 21 s and local agent shells time out: CI's workflow sets none of REBAR_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, OPENCODE_SESSION_ID, or SESSION_ID.\n\nWhy the per-comment check exists: story recent-wholesome-fulmar (6d95718080c, 2026-08-28) added `emit_cross_session_warning` to each single-ticket public library call (`comment`, `edit_ticket`, `link`, `set_file_impact`, ...) for direct `import rebar` callers. It explicitly keeps bulk operations silent and has outer surfaces hold `suppress_cross_session_warning()` so they advise once. `import_tickets` was not considered; it reuses those public single-ticket calls internally, so it inherited one detector read per row.\n\nThe check is redundant inside import:\n- Every ticket the import's passes 2a-2d touch was created by this same import in pass 1. A new ticket has no claimed_session; statuses are replayed later, in pass 2e, through `transition_compute`, which does not emit. Push is deferred until the end of the import.\n- The CLI path (`rebar store import`) already runs under `suppress_cross_session_warning()` (`_cli/_execute.py`), and `import` is not in the CLI's cross-session allowlist; MCP tools are wrapped the same way. Only direct library callers pay the per-row read.\n\nFix: `import_tickets` holds `suppress_cross_session_warning()` across its write passes, the same guard the CLI and MCP surfaces already hold. Single-ticket library calls outside import keep their warning unchanged. No opcert code touched.","timestamp":1793793813039225001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Evidence 2026-11-04 PST: `tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass` crashed its xdist worker in the integration tier of `make verify` (worktree fix-caudata), and alone it hit the 300 s pytest-timeout with the stack in `_lib_mutations.comment` -> `_lib_warn.emit_cross_session_warning` -> `show_ticket` -> `config.load_config`. Paired runs with --timeout=1800 at host load average ~28: base `8f12601dfdb` 302.78 s call, `1e585fdd0f5` 316.61 s call (1 sample each), both passing. So at this load the test exceeds the default 300 s budget on main independent of that change.","timestamp":1793796424576399001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verification of fix commit (Change-Id I89f8b654399acb562742e575227645f4696fd66c), 2026-11-04 PST:\n- New test test_import_git_process_count_does_not_depend_on_acting_session: fails without the fix (125 git processes with a session id vs 100 without, 6 rows), passes with it.\n- Benchmark test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass, run alone: before 310.0 s wall, timeout, load 28-36; after 79.6 s wall, pass, load 19-21.\n- n=50 import with a session id: 120 git processes / 15.8 s before, 19 / 2.5 s after (same as the no-session run).\n- Import, cross-session and reconciler suites: 3966 passed. make lint and make typecheck pass; import_tickets complexity unchanged at its baseline of 45; import_ndjson.py is 368 lines.\n- make verify, default tier: 20762 passed, 2 failed in 2 h 2 min at load 24-28. Both failures are CLI facade tests that also fail on origin/main without this change when run after another CLI test in one process: filed bald-diagnostic-cricket.\n- Integration tier run separately: 202 passed, 1 failed in 8 min 29 s at load 25-40. The benchmark no longer times out. The failure is the live-Jira test_delete_permission_probe index-visibility flake: filed bottom-hawkish-sunfish.","timestamp":1793805058483148001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793789358020115001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3482ea5d-6bfc-468f-b80e-454daf2953f7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2698-ff06-5f35-463c"},{"link_uuid":"ccc57a14-1ddd-4e5f-b442-ddf3db6c9be3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1561-dc08-688f-49ae"},{"link_uuid":"26505f53-c343-4599-b5e5-ffe21ed3a1ca","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"726c-93e3-df00-4f4b"},{"link_uuid":"e273f3bf-77a3-4aaa-8e8a-115057d16ad5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7a10-4595-1c7e-4286"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass` (integration tier, n=3000 tickets with 1 comment each) hit the 300 s pytest-timeout on 2026-11-04 on a macOS host at load average 25-33. That happened twice: once in `make verify`'s integration tier (xdist worker gw2 \"node down: Not properly terminated\"), and again when run alone.\n\nThe timeout stack was in import's comment pass: `rebar._io.import_ndjson.import_tickets` (line 290) -> `rebar._lib_mutations.comment` (line 74) -> `emit_cross_session_warning` (`src/rebar/_lib_warn.py:59`) -> `cross_session_warning_for` (`src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py:54`) -> `show_ticket` -> `_reads._fresh` -> `ensure_fresh` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:221`), waiting on a `git` child.\n\n`ensure_fresh` spawns `git rev-parse --verify <branch>` before it checks its 60 s marker throttle, so every comment imported pays a full ticket read plus at least 1 git child process for an advisory cross-session warning. On an import of n comments that is n extra processes, and the cost scales with host load.\n\nThe comment path has existed since 2026-08-27 (`65208a7ef81`, `6d95718080c`). It was found while verifying `quartzitic-deathful-needletail`, whose change touches only `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`.\n\n## Next check\n\nCount the git child processes per imported comment (a Popen counter around `rebar.import_tickets` with n=50). Then compare against an import with the cross-session warning disabled, to test whether the warning read accounts for the per-comment process cost.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] The git child-process count for importing n comments is measured and recorded on this ticket, with and without the cross-session warning read.\n  provenance: environment=local macOS dev host, unmodified origin/main 30f06afc412, n=50 import into a temporary repo; principal=Rebar Bot Nava agent session; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=simulation — a Popen counter wrapped around rebar.import_tickets, run with and without an acting session id, with results (120 vs 19 git processes) recorded in the root-cause comment of 2026-11-04.\n- [x] Importing n comments does not start a git child process per comment for the cross-session warning; verified by a test that counts Popen calls during a small import.\n\n## Fix\n\n`import_tickets` (`src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py`) holds `suppress_cross_session_warning()` across its write passes, as the CLI and MCP surfaces already do. Every ticket those passes touch was created unclaimed by Pass 1 of the same import, so the advisory read could never fire. Regression test: `tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batching.py::test_import_git_process_count_does_not_depend_on_acting_session`. Landed as Gerrit 3304, merged `02f78b847d2`.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py","reason":"import holds the cross-session suppression guard across its write passes"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batching.py","reason":"regression test: import git-process count does not depend on the acting session"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1561-dc08-688f-49ae"],["relates_to","726c-93e3-df00-4f4b"],["relates_to","7a10-4595-1c7e-4286"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6582d993-6e6b-4031-b507-cd924388b5e3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"571b-f552-5fa7-4b74","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Import comment pass starts a git process per comment for the cross-session warning","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b53699f6-ec7f-48a2-9d67-3a907b017550","840160e7-4a08-4c36-9b3c-58e4bcecf070","eea00abc-74d6-4014-9253-104ca12b951f","b9ef343a-8d87-4e3e-ad48-b9a973efae0f","08ec9158-0578-4d6d-b1ce-72f2ab09e317","26505f53-c343-4599-b5e5-ffe21ed3a1ca","d3ee1f50-7abf-4369-90e3-4b9e65e3f50c","9de6a2a4-e41c-4ad4-b32e-5696ab87009a","5becc05c-0015-46a1-8b29-be4f42c74013","e273f3bf-77a3-4aaa-8e8a-115057d16ad5","6582d993-6e6b-4031-b507-cd924388b5e3","b1f2629a-9a64-4cbb-b0a9-95b100b744a4"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793811278081781002,"uuid":"24d40de9-0258-4a6b-8fc9-6fdfc2a91530"}